snapshot-wiki (0.1.0) unstable; urgency=low

  * Initial packaging: the SnapshOT Wiki, a MkDocs Material site built at
    package build time (mkdocs build --strict) and installed to
    /usr/share/snapshot/wiki for offline use from file://.
  * hooks/snapshot_wiki.py validates the page front-matter against data/
    (menu folders, PICERL phases, ATT&CK for ICS tactics and techniques,
    protocols), generates the navigation, the tool, folder, tactic, protocol
    and matrix pages, the facts boxes and the graph data.
  * Vendor vis-network 10.1.2 and the iframe-worker 1.0.4 shim (offline
    search on file://); see assets/vendor/ORIGIN.md.
  * Graphs: zoom in, zoom out and full-screen buttons at the top right; the
    mouse wheel scrolls the page and zooms only in full screen.
  * Ship /etc/firefox/policies/policies.json and
    /etc/firefox-esr/snapshot-quiet.js so Firefox ESR makes no unsolicited
    connections and opens the wiki as its home page. Remote Settings, which
    the pinned ESR 140 has no policy for, is kept off the wire by resolving
    its three hosts to loopback (network.dns.localDomains), as are the
    new-tab feeds that download its attachments; scripts/check-firefox-quiet.sh,
    run against the image's pinned firefox-esr, captures no packet in 45
    seconds and finds no policy the pinned Firefox does not know.
  * Divert xfce4-helpers' /etc/xdg/xfce4/helpers.rc and link it to
    /usr/share/snapshot-wiki/xfce4-helpers.rc (the same keys, WebBrowser
    pinned to debian-sensible-browser); not shipped at the diverted path,
    which would collide with xfce4-helpers' conffile. Ship
    /etc/xdg/mimeapps.list with firefox-esr.desktop for HTML and http(s)
    links. Depend on sensible-utils, which provides sensible-browser (it is
    Priority important and already in the debootstrap base; the dependency
    keeps the default-browser chain from resting on that).

 -- Blackbird Cyber <snapshot@example.invalid>  Tue, 06 Oct 2026 00:00:00 +0000
